  "tail_text": "NotImplementedError`, which needs to be fixed. Additionally, the LRU cache is not evicting the correct key when the capacity is reached. We need to implement an LRU cache that correctly evicts the least recently used item when the capacity is exceeded.\n\nHere is the updated `unicaa01_p02_panic/main.py` file:\n\nunicaa01_p02_panic/main.py\n```\n\"\"\"Fixed LRU.\"\"\"\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\nclass LRU:\n    def __init__(self, cap):\n        self.cap = cap\n        self.data = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, k):\n        if k not in self.data:\n            return -1\n        self.data.move_to_end(k)\n        return self.data[k]\n\n    def put(self, k, v):\n        if k in self.data:\n            self.data.move_to_end(k)\n        self.data[k] = v\n        if len(self.data) > self.cap:\n            self.data.popitem(last=False)\n\ndef demo():\n    c = LRU(2)\n    c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); c.get(1); c.put(3, 3)\n    return [c.get(1), c.get(2)]\n```\n\nExplanation of changes:\n1. **Import `OrderedDict`**: We use `OrderedDict` from the `collections` module to maintain the order of insertion.\n2. **Fix `get()` method**: The `get()` method now checks if the key exists in the cache. If it does, it moves the key to the end of the `OrderedDict` to mark it as recently used and returns the value. If the key does not exist, it returns `-1`.\n3. **Fix `put()` method**: The `put()` method now checks if the key already exists in the cache. If it does, it moves the key to the end of the `OrderedDict` to mark it as recently used. It then updates the value. If the key does not exist, it adds the key-value pair to the cache. If the cache exceeds its capacity, it removes the least recently used item (the first item in the `OrderedDict`).\n4. **Demo function**: The `demo()` function demonstrates the usage of the `LRU` class and returns the expected results.",
  "full_completion_text": "NotImplementedError`, which needs to be fixed. Additionally, the LRU cache is not evicting the correct key when the capacity is reached. We need to implement an LRU cache that correctly evicts the least recently used item when the capacity is exceeded.\n\nHere is the updated `unicaa01_p02_panic/main.py` file:\n\nunicaa01_p02_panic/main.py\n```\n\"\"\"Fixed LRU.\"\"\"\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\nclass LRU:\n    def __init__(self, cap):\n        self.cap = cap\n        self.data = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, k):\n        if k not in self.data:\n            return -1\n        self.data.move_to_end(k)\n        return self.data[k]\n\n    def put(self, k, v):\n        if k in self.data:\n            self.data.move_to_end(k)\n        self.data[k] = v\n        if len(self.data) > self.cap:\n            self.data.popitem(last=False)\n\ndef demo():\n    c = LRU(2)\n    c.put(1, 1); c.put(2, 2); c.get(1); c.put(3, 3)\n    return [c.get(1), c.get(2)]\n```\n\nExplanation of changes:\n1. **Import `OrderedDict`**: We use `OrderedDict` from the `collections` module to maintain the order of insertion.\n2. **Fix `get()` method**: The `get()` method now checks if the key exists in the cache. If it does, it moves the key to the end of the `OrderedDict` to mark it as recently used and returns the value. If the key does not exist, it returns `-1`.\n3. **Fix `put()` method**: The `put()` method now checks if the key already exists in the cache. If it does, it moves the key to the end of the `OrderedDict` to mark it as recently used. It then updates the value. If the key does not exist, it adds the key-value pair to the cache. If the cache exceeds its capacity, it removes the least recently used item (the first item in the `OrderedDict`).\n4. **Demo function**: The `demo()` function demonstrates the usage of the `LRU` class and returns the expected results.",
